%I A401475 #16 Nov 03 2026 14:25:39
%S A401475 2,7,37,265,2396,26118,332723,4845044,79327314,1441840473,28797904948,
%T A401475 626815406988,14765197821831,374200770218086,10151746125999166
%N A401475 Number of cokernel-closed, idempotent split, full, additive subcategories of the category of finite-dimensional complex representations of a uniformly oriented A_n quiver.
%C A401475 The subcategories are closed under finite direct sums and direct summands. Cokernel closure means that the cokernel of every morphism between objects of the subcategory also belongs to the subcategory.
%C A401475 In the notation of Mazorchuk and Xu, a(n) = r(n-1).
%C A401475 SageMath code for computing the terms is included at the end of the arXiv preprint by Mazorchuk and Xu.
%H A401475 Henning Krause and Balduin Stoye, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22649">Multisets of finite intervals and a universal category of poset representations</a>, arXiv:2601.22649 [math.RT], 2026.
%H A401475 Volodymyr Mazorchuk and Shuoyang Xu, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.07999">On the number of cokernel-closed additive subcategories for uniformly oriented A_n quivers</a>, arXiv:2610.07999 [math.CO], 2026.
%H A401475 Shuoyang Xu, <a href="/A401475/a401475.txt">Python program</a>
%e A401475 For n = 1, the two subcategories are the zero subcategory and the whole category of finite-dimensional complex vector spaces, so a(1) = 2.
%o A401475 (Python) # See Links
%Y A401475 Cf. A000108 (Catalan numbers), A393920 (number of extension-closed subcategories).
%K A401475 nonn,more,new
%O A401475 1,1
